+# Story 23-1: Unified Plugin SDK Core
+
+## Business Context
+
+All Axiathon extension points (parsers, connectors, enrichers, dissectors, notification channels, response actions) need a shared SDK so plugin developers use one trait hierarchy, one manifest format, and one set of tooling regardless of plugin type. Without this foundation, every subsequent plugin story (23.2-23.14) and all first-party plugins (Stories 2.8-2.12) cannot proceed. This is the SDK that the Claroty xDome plugin (Story 2.8.1) -- the primary validation target -- will be built against.
+
+The spike workspace has a complete, tested plugin SDK with 5 sub-crates and 6 working first-party plugins. This story ports the spike to production with key improvements: structured `PluginError` (replacing anyhow), extended `PluginManifest` (config_schema, OCSF metadata, signatures), JSON Schema config validation via the `jsonschema` crate, and the `async_trait` decision (native async fn is NOT object-safe with `Box<dyn Trait>` as of Rust 1.85).
+
+**Jira:** DPGD-114
+**Points:** 8
+**Implementation artifact:** `axiathon/_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/approved/wave-1/23-1-unified-plugin-sdk-core.md`
+
+## Technical Guardrails
+
+- **Workspace layout:** All 6 SDK crates are root workspace members (Cargo does not support nested workspaces). Directory structure at `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/` with sub-crate directories: core, ingestion, network, notification, action.
+- **async_trait required:** Native async fn in traits is NOT object-safe with `Box<dyn Trait>` in Rust 1.85. All async traits needing dyn dispatch (`AxiathonPlugin`, `ConnectorPlugin`, `NotificationChannel`, `ResponseAction`) must use `#[async_trait]`. Sync traits (`ParserPlugin`, `ProtocolDissector`) use native Rust traits.
+- **Dependency boundary:** SDK crates depend on `axiathon-types` (crates.io target), NOT `axiathon-core`. Interim: use `axiathon-core` until Story 1.21 lands.
+- **Error handling:** `PluginError` enum with thiserror (not anyhow). Different variants trigger different runtime behaviors (ConfigInvalid -> reject config, HealthCheckFailed -> degrade status, NotFound -> 404).
+- **Object safety:** All plugin traits MUST be object-safe (`Box<dyn Trait>` must compile). Verified via compile tests.
+- **Config validation:** `PluginManifest::validate_config()` uses `jsonschema` crate (20-470x faster than alternatives).
+
+**Key files to create:**
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/Cargo.toml` and `src/lib.rs` (facade)
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/core/src/{lib,identity,manifest,lifecycle,health,error,config}.rs`
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/ingestion/src/lib.rs`
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/network/src/lib.rs`
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/notification/src/lib.rs`
+- `crates/axiathon-plugin-sdk/action/src/lib.rs`
+
